#: ../smart-base/L2/collab/processes/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:23
#. Diagram element documentation
#, fuzzy
msgid "One pass over one L2 DAK component: the agent edits it, runs its checker, renders and stages it with a before/after, and hands it on; review forks off beside the hand-on and never holds it up (adjudication is QA, not a gate). Called once per component pass by each authoring track of l2-dak-authoring.bpmn (Process_L2Dak). Only the call's inputs differ between components (skill l2-component-edit-review, \"The inputs, per component\"): - component: personas and user scenarios (C2, C3), business processes (C4), core data elements and glossary (C5) with their terminology bindings, decision-support and scheduling logic (C6, C7), indicators and requirements (C8, C9); - authoring skill: l2-dak-authoring, bpmn-authoring, dmn-authoring or terminology-management, named on the calling activity, so it joins this process's skills along the call path (review-task.bpmn's scoped composition); - renderer and diff: what the reviewer sees, before and after; - checker: the mechanical checks the agent runs before asking anyone; - reviewing role: the person who takes this process's reviewer lane for the call."
msgstr "Un paso sobre un componente de DAK L2: el agente lo edita, ejecuta su verificador, lo renderiza y lo escalona con un antes/después, y lo entrega; revisa los tenedores al lado de la mano y nunca lo sostiene (adjudicación es QA, no una puerta). Llamado una vez por componente pasa por cada pista de autor de l2-dak-authoring.bpmn (Process_L2Dak). Sólo las entradas de la llamada difieren entre los componentes (skill l2-componente-edit-review, \"The inputs, per compon\"): - componente: personas y escenarios de usuario (C2, C3), procesos de negocio (C4), elementos de datos básicos y glosario (C5) con sus enlaces terminológicos, lógica de apoyo a la decisión y programación (C6, C7), indicadores y requisitos (C8, C9); - habilidad de autor: l2-dak-authoring, bpn-authoring, dmn-authoring o gestión terminológica (C8);"

#: ../smart-base/L2/collab/processes/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:159
#. Diagram label
#, fuzzy
msgid "reject"
msgstr "rechazar"

#: ../smart-base/L2/collab/processes/l2-component-edit-review.bpmn:85
#. Diagram element documentation
#, fuzzy
msgid "Render the component the way its reviewer reads it (column \"renderer and diff\"): the BPMN diagram (render:bpmn) with a visual-diff picture; the DMN decision table (smart-base-transform.py dmn2html) with each rule's L1 citation; the data dictionary's term diff (dak-data-dictionary-diff.ts) and the chosen wireframe of each form; personas, scenarios and requirements as a prose diff. Commit to the feature branch so it is staged as branches/<slug>/ on the platform's just-the-docs site (for smart-base, a folio-assistant staging re-pin, never the IG's /deploy), and make the before/after preview here so it exists when review starts."
msgstr "Renderiza el componente de la forma en que lo lee su revisor (columna \"renderer and diff\": el diagrama BPMN (render:bpmn) con una imagen visual-diff; la tabla de decisiones DMN (smart-base-transform.py dmn2html) con la cita L1 de cada regla; el término diff del diccionario de datos (dak-data-dictionary-diff.ts) y el marco de alambre elegido de cada forma; personas, escenarios y requisitos como un diff de prosa. Comprométete con la rama de características por lo que se representa como ramas/<slug>/ en el sitio justo-el-docs de la plataforma (para smart-base, un folio-assistant stating re-pin, nunca el IG's /deploy), y haz la vista previa/después aquí para que exista cuando comience la revisión."

